# Impeccable Distill Rules

Distill means removing unnecessary elements and focusing on what matters most.

---

## Core Principle

Less, but better.

If something does not help the user → remove it.

---

## Remove Unnecessary

- Remove:
  - redundant text
  - extra labels
  - unnecessary icons
  - duplicated information
- Avoid clutter

---

## Prioritize Core Information

- Each screen should have a clear main purpose
- Highlight only the most important content

---

## Simplify Content

- Use shorter text
- Avoid long explanations
- Use concise language

---

## Reduce Duplication

- Do not repeat the same information
- Keep content clean and minimal

---

## Simplify Layout

- Reduce number of elements
- Avoid complex UI structures
- Keep layout easy to scan

---

## Clarity Through Reduction

- Removing elements should improve clarity
- Do not remove essential information

---

## Constraints

- Do not change business logic
- Maintain usability
- Keep UI readable and clear

---

## Goal

The UI should feel:

- simple
- clean
- focused
- efficient
